rl": "https://news.google.?oc=5"}, {"title": "Tennessee US House District 9: Republican Taylor and Democrat Pearson set for general election", "source": "Tennessee Lookout", "published": "2026-08-06T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": -7.54, "prior_sd": 5.11, "poll_margin": -5.5, "poll_sd": 12.22, "poll_weight": 0.15, "fundamentals": {"margin": -0.69, "lean": -9.0, "environment": 8.2, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": 0.11}, "rating_margin": -12.11, "sigma_race": 6.0, "sigma_total": 6.82, "baseline_margin": -7.24, "analyst_adjustment": -1.76, "key_factors": ["Redistricting split the majority-Black district, giving Republicans a favorable map", "Expert ratings uniformly call the seat a Republican flip, mostly Likely or Solid R", "The only poll (Democratic-sponsored, early September) shows Taylor up just 4, better for Pearson than ratings imply", "Pearson has outraised Taylor and holds more cash, but Taylor has far more outside support"], "rationale": "The redrawn district's Republican lean, a unanimous Likely/Solid R rating consensus, and Polymarket pricing near 88% Republican point to a clear Taylor advantage. The single early poll showing a 4-point race and Pearson's fundraising edge temper that somewhat, but not enough to move the seat out of Likely R.", "watch": "A late surge in Democratic outside spending or new polling showing Pearson within a few points could tighten the race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Steve Cohen (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Tennessee's 9th District is an open seat after Steve Cohen's retirement, and a new state map split the state's only majority-Black district, putting Republican Brent Taylor against Democrat Justin Pearson. Every major rating outlet calls the seat a Republican flip, ranging from Likely R to Safe R, and prediction markets price Taylor near 88%. Pearson has raised more money than Taylor and holds a cash advantage, though Taylor benefits from substantially more outside spending. The lone poll, a Democratic-sponsored survey from early September, showed Taylor ahead by four points, closer than the ratings suggest. The fundamentals still favor Republicans in this redrawn, Republican-leaning district, but Pearson's fundraising and the narrow poll keep some uncertainty in the outlook.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1065, "margin": -7.68}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.132, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1308, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1301, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1022, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0793, "margin": -9.0}]}